---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Gradient Notes and the ideas collected here.">
  <article class="shell about-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>A place to make ideas precise.</h1>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          Gradient Notes is a public working notebook about the theory and practice
          of modern learning systems.
        </p>

        <p>
          The subjects here overlap on purpose. Probability gives us a language for
          uncertainty. Optimization turns objectives into procedures. Language models
          test those procedures at scale. Reinforcement learning asks what changes when
          the data depends on our own decisions.
        </p>

        <p>
          Most entries begin with a small question and end when the answer is clear
          enough to reuse. Expect derivations, diagrams made out of equations, compact
          experiments, and occasional corrections.
        </p>

        <h2>Colophon</h2>
        <p>
          This site is built with Astro and plain CSS. Pages are rendered at build time;
          there is no client-side JavaScript. Mathematics is typeset with KaTeX, and the
          whole site remains usable as a set of static files.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="about-aside">
        <p>Principles</p>
        <ol>
          <li><span>01</span> Show the derivation.</li>
          <li><span>02</span> Name the assumptions.</li>
          <li><span>03</span> Prefer small examples.</li>
          <li><span>04</span> Correct mistakes in public.</li>
        </ol>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

